            <ArticleTitle>Improvement of pain therapy in laboratory mice.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>6-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Pain of minor grades is difficult to detect in laboratory mice, because mice hide signs of injury and suffering. Low-grade post-operative pain was detected by continuous measurements of heart beat rate and variability, as well as nesting behaviours. Pain relief regimens with non-steroidal anti inflammatory drugs were shown to be effective.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
